  "query_preview": "(Monday through Thursday)...\nThe slow cooling trend will continue for Monday and Tuesday with\nsome model differences for Wednesday and Thursday with the\nstrength and placement of the high across the central and \nsouthern Rockies westward to California. High temperatures for \nnext Wednesday will be generally within a few degrees of average \nnear the coast to 4 to 8 degrees above average for inland areas. \nHigh temperatures for next Wednesday will range from the mid 70s \nto lower 80s near the coast to the mid 90s to 105 for the Inland \nEmpire with 110 to 114 for the lower deserts. \n\nLow temperatures will cool a few degrees on Monday and again on\nTuesday, then change little for Wednesday and Thursday. Low\ntemperatures on Wednesday will be mostly in the 60s and lower 70s\nfor the coast and valleys, in the 70s for the Apple and Lucerne \nValleys, and in the mid 80s to lower 90s for the lower deserts.\n\nThere will be moderate HeatRisk for next Wednesday for the inland\nvalleys and mountain elevations below 5500 feet with moderate to\nmajor HeatRisk for the deserts. \n\nDepending on the placement of the high, there could be some\nincrease in moisture from the east during the latter half of next\nweek. Through Friday of next week, NBM chances for measurable\nprecipitation are greatest over the mountains for next Thursday\nafternoon at 10 to 15 percent.",
